From: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] autogen: take the version from the changelog, not git

autogen.sh asks `git describe` for the version and only falls back to
doc/changelog when that fails. Buildroot unpacks the release tarball,
which has no .git, so git walks up the directory tree and answers for
whatever repository the build directory happens to sit in. Built from a
Buildroot_MiSTer checkout, `gpm -v` printed that repository's tag
(v2026.10.23-beta) and the build depended on the host's git state.

A release tarball's version is the changelog's, so always use it.

Upstream: not sent (gpm is unmaintained upstream).

Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
---
 autogen.sh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/autogen.sh
+++ b/autogen.sh
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 
 [ -d config ] || mkdir config
 
-version=$(git describe 2>/dev/null)
+version=
 
 # No git? use changelog information
 if [ -z "$version" ]; then
